+      <p class="why-it-matters">A price that traders use to forecast the price itself makes the forecast and the price depend on each other. This lesson states a linear-normal one-period model in which that loop closes exactly. The rational-expectations equilibrium is a fixed point of a map on the forecast's coefficients, a value that the map sends to itself (Proposition 2.2). The fixed point has a closed form. Iterating the map from an arbitrary start converges only under a condition on the slopes. The lab checks the fixed point and the error ratio of the iteration in exact arithmetic. The model is a stated special case, and the lesson makes no claim about any market.</p>
